.TH std::ranges::join_view::iterator 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::ranges::join_view::iterator \- std::ranges::join_view::iterator

.SH Synopsis
template< bool Const >  \fI(since C++20)\fP
class /*iterator*/      (exposition only*)

The return type of join_view::begin, and of join_view::end when both the outer range V and
the inner range ranges::range_reference_t<V> satisfy common_range and the parent join_view
is a forward_range.

If V is not a simple view (e.g. if ranges::iterator_t<const V> is invalid or different
from ranges::iterator_t<V>), Const is true for iterators returned from the const
overloads, and false otherwise. If V is a simple view, Const is true if and only if
ranges::range_reference_t<V> is a reference.

